e above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|x|\\\\sqrt{6{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{6}}{|\\\\sqrt{6}x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\sqrt{6}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{6}}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\sqrt{6}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{6}}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186250177 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"345d0dd8-1722-50e6-996a-3145ed9fa4cc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{7}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247894} {:answer/id #uuid \"795dfd60-9293-54b9-a133-af67359f3625\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248490} {:answer/id #uuid \"a6deadf7-ef59-56ac-a86b-d7bdb56e7adc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\\\\sqrt{7}\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248908} {:answer/id #uuid \"afa04312-a9ee-53e6-8294-76266301a3a4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248999} {:answer/id #uuid \"d0c6dca0-cfeb-5ddf-b8cf-96bba1eee175\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{7}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186249278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d0c6dca0-cfeb-5ddf-b8cf-96bba1eee175\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{7}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186249278} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ae56369a-9dc7-56a8-9b42-9abf878339d0\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186249978}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"37dfb0c1-ed42-5302-8312-3364def8fc97\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-114055\" :question/problem \"Calculate $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{7}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{7}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x=\\\\int \\\\frac{7\\\\sqrt{7}}{|\\\\sqrt{7}x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{7}x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\\\sqrt{7}x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\\\sqrt{7}x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=\\\\sqrt{7}\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{7}}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{7}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{7\\\\sqrt{7}}{|\\\\sqrt{7}x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{7}x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =7\\\\sqrt{7}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{7}}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =7\\\\sqrt{7}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{7}}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =7\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =7\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{7}x)+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186250178 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"06349d8e-8391-574b-b6ee-d09717af159e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\sqrt{8}\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247480} {:answer/id #uuid \"28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{8}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247786} {:answer/id #uuid \"4b4c8ae4-b8b1-5ed2-b232-73c90f37ed26\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{8}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248097} {:answer/id #uuid \"97ffb8aa-ac92-5db2-a3d4-4a6b34576f59\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{8}}{8}\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248778} {:answer/id #uuid \"b9b1dd01-2ffe-53eb-9456-1dfad676593b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}\\\\left(\\\\frac{x}{\\\\sqrt{8}}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186249084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"28b08c9d-77c7-5bea-8de3-24e47c4a6b22\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{8}x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247786} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f124bfeb-924c-5974-b5d6-5bac9d8b7458\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186250090}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"d978df6a-8484-5ed1-885e-b4758185514d\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-114056\" :question/problem \"Calculate $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|x|\\\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|x|\\\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x=\\\\int \\\\frac{8\\\\sqrt{8}}{|\\\\sqrt{8}x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\\\sqrt{8}x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\\\sqrt{8}x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=\\\\sqrt{8}\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{8}}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|x|\\\\sqrt{8{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{8\\\\sqrt{8}}{|\\\\sqrt{8}x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{8}x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\sqrt{8}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{8}}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\sqrt{8}\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{8}}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =8\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(\\\\sqrt{8}x)+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186250179 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"20eeed43-06fc-5a51-a569-cc359295eeb2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(50x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247713} {:answer/id #uuid \"23a4faf6-7048-5692-877b-730a3aa48b44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(10x)+C\" :db/id 17592186247737} {:answer/id #uuid \"860a98b5-c89e-5a98-a319-70c942ace928\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(10x)+C\" :db/id 17592186248619} {:answer/id #uuid \"c1ea824c-8f8e-5257-ae08-86f03dfd7210\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(10x)+C\" :db/id 17592186249149} {:answer/id #uuid \"d7024181-5209-53f4-9e77-1d70e6a37869\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(x)+C\" :db/id 17592186249324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c1ea824c-8f8e-5257-ae08-86f03dfd7210\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(10x)+C\" :db/id 17592186249149} :answer-field/id #uuid \"1249c5e2-b95a-56a8-9562-7cfa27416496\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186249702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"1386e5e4-c2d1-50fc-ab2e-40d086cf4081\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-114057\" :question/problem \"Calculate $$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{100{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{100{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x=\\\\int \\\\frac{50}{|10x|\\\\sqrt{(10x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $10x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=10x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=10\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{10}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{100{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{50}{|10x|\\\\sqrt{(10x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =50\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{10}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =50\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{10}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(10x)+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186332729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"26bff1d2-1a1f-5568-b606-c926ad4e222e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186330288} {:answer/id #uuid \"38f382b6-b9e0-5d37-bb15-bf2017958200\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186330460} {:answer/id #uuid \"88b1a168-dccc-5c24-aa5c-58eef11e4b53\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)+C\" :db/id 17592186331165} {:answer/id #uuid \"8a671a08-acf6-51a4-a4b1-a79a1a8a1a19\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(16x)}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186331179} {:answer/id #uuid \"c1c62bda-b0cb-5477-843f-9e7f08c270e5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186331672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"c1c62bda-b0cb-5477-843f-9e7f08c270e5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186331672} :answer-field/id #uuid \"2ed515ce-b125-59ef-ba87-1982f7680cc3\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186332279}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"cd302e3c-b39d-509b-8801-010e64d93a57\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-49519\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{4|x|\\\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{4|x|\\\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}=\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|4x|\\\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $4x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=4\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{4|x|\\\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4x|\\\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186332740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4b0edf81-9914-5a0f-b9b6-d58d70540093\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186330630} {:answer/id #uuid \"70cf07b2-a48c-5c20-b1ad-493648041c3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186330962} {:answer/id #uuid \"9a56a3d4-f0db-5dee-8e1b-e1e7174dd979\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(3x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186331338} {:answer/id #uuid \"a43c7a93-7056-56e0-adc4-8cc368c5eac5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(9x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186331423} {:answer/id #uuid \"e8c453d1-3b22-5ee0-8261-9dc453f931aa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186331996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e8c453d1-3b22-5ee0-8261-9dc453f931aa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186331996} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b3ccce72-f1f2-5395-8899-d57e02ead31c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186332512}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"751e8889-464b-57e5-9446-01158bf809c1\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-49554\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{3|x|\\\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{3|x|\\\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}=\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|3x|\\\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $3x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=3\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{3|x|\\\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|3x|\\\\sqrt{(3x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{3}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186332741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1afb9d8c-3f67-5355-93d6-a9093bad7dae\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(6x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186330187} {:answer/id #uuid \"3226e3a9-ff07-580d-875b-1db26197856a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186330391} {:answer/id #uuid \"d697edf8-7533-5458-807b-5604ad7429ef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)+C\" :db/id 17592186331847} {:answer/id #uuid \"d72cc629-030b-503a-b49e-63c0be8afa3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186331853} {:answer/id #uuid \"d885db49-c6b0-5c70-8dc4-c09546b4b009\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C\" :db/id 17592186331870}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d72cc629-030b-503a-b49e-63c0be8afa3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186331853} :answer-field/id #uuid \"89604dd1-6f4e-5479-bb62-31a5924f3f5e\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186332441}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"8067bb84-25f1-5b9a-af1c-e522b42ac4cd\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-49555\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{6|x|\\\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{6|x|\\\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}=\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=6\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{6|x|\\\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186335976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4c842fc6-bdb7-5fd1-95ec-a8a6c5c213af\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C\" :db/id 17592186333694} {:answer/id #uuid \"8817bce9-1d12-59f6-a5d1-e12cf7bf9ea0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186334193} {:answer/id #uuid \"d4994be2-56ea-5429-8d7d-0f2980d19115\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(49x)}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186334851} {:answer/id #uuid \"d5ef86d7-cffa-55cc-8343-9157ea5e011e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)}{49}+C\" :db/id 17592186334864} {:answer/id #uuid \"eff32ea7-4fa2-5bab-91d2-777e88bff4bf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(49x)+C\" :db/id 17592186335089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4c842fc6-bdb7-5fd1-95ec-a8a6c5c213af\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C\" :db/id 17592186333694} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ebde86f4-5f82-5ab1-8866-0726b82f2be1\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335652}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"1090f68a-a5e7-5187-bfa4-8579cbfba1e4\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-69475\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{7\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|7x|\\\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{7\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|7x|\\\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}=7\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|7x|\\\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $7x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=7x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=7\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{7}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}7\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7x|\\\\sqrt{(7x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x & =7\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{7}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\text{arcsec}(7x)+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186335977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"48ed7e88-42a3-5874-867c-a70eb196b8de\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)+C\" :db/id 17592186333661} {:answer/id #uuid \"8bc52df5-2130-5724-8f9a-3900402db0a3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186334237} {:answer/id #uuid \"961ad6bb-bcc5-55c8-bf62-b1d0251abaec\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186334325} {:answer/id #uuid \"d33c5bc0-c46c-505d-825e-d5fb312cca88\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(3x)}{81}+C\" :db/id 17592186334839} {:answer/id #uuid \"d9456840-7b87-506e-b8e7-b50a98cb1b55\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(3x)+C\" :db/id 17592186334895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8bc52df5-2130-5724-8f9a-3900402db0a3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186334237} :answer-field/id #uuid \"2ae037e8-4b57-5061-96fb-95244295292c\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335317}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"ea572027-5f6a-57b6-b534-919c7f5636f2\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-69477\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{3\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}=3\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|9x|\\\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $9x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=9x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=9\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|9x|\\\\sqrt{(9x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x & =3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(9x)}{3}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186342066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"12a76728-b839-5d06-89f1-9934eae3f027\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186339291} {:answer/id #uuid \"665fe7b3-58d5-51b3-a6e6-d098ccd5df2d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{36}+C\" :db/id 17592186340029} {:answer/id #uuid \"689ac8e4-68fd-56b3-a68a-d04dadd83f44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186340060} {:answer/id #uuid \"926a2dfc-a131-5563-ba53-5afa24278c9d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(36x)}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186340442} {:answer/id #uuid \"e3ae6232-f8ce-5ece-a30d-6e27d814267f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(36x)+C\" :db/id 17592186341146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"689ac8e4-68fd-56b3-a68a-d04dadd83f44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186340060} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c6e02fde-8f73-598e-a892-0518e56b81c6\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341728}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"8cd85d7e-9002-5474-aae0-35e5eb480c8e\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73715\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{3\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3\\\\,\\\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}=3\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $6x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=6x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=6\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|6x|\\\\sqrt{(6x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x & =3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(6x)}{2}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186342067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5be9359f-ea8b-563c-9bb9-6b1a6826176f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186339961} {:answer/id #uuid \"64bf2439-df5c-5f13-8e13-540b1d44c9d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)+C\" :db/id 17592186340020} {:answer/id #uuid \"81d073cc-887d-5b6a-aeab-6cecc28a4382\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)+C\" :db/id 17592186340297} {:answer/id #uuid \"95b7f420-0b28-5282-a657-40d893b628dd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arctan}(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186340478} {:answer/id #uuid \"d5244b0b-6f4f-5504-8207-05f6294fbb10\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arctan}(4x)+C\" :db/id 17592186341015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"5be9359f-ea8b-563c-9bb9-6b1a6826176f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186339961} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d91ba1e9-1dd8-5d35-a35f-ac59fd9e8143\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341764}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"78df4070-47af-5dba-93f4-a34eb10c085e\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73716\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|4x|\\\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"This integral resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $4x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=4\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4x|\\\\sqrt{(4x)^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186342068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"14690a52-f522-5cec-90d3-9f420e7fc080\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\,\\\\text{arctan}(5x)+C\" :db/id 17592186339311} {:answer/id #uuid \"5da47576-8911-5b68-868f-555462fcef8e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C\" :db/id 17592186339968} {:answer/id #uuid \"6ec5d84f-e713-5832-b748-a0e4c715f798\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arctan}(5x)}{5}+C\" :db/id 17592186340111} {:answer/id #uuid \"7b9a50aa-ecbb-5989-afe3-1d8c3cdb9d07\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C\" :db/id 17592186340239} {:answer/id #uuid \"99ab830d-95ff-5734-ab2f-bab2f3570815\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5\\\\,\\\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C\" :db/id 17592186340514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"5da47576-8911-5b68-868f-555462fcef8e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C\" :db/id 17592186339968} :answer-field/id #uuid \"0d389694-7fb3-5b9c-b985-67d93a5095c2\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341402}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"6b1a4da5-f80f-5816-895f-0dc3214bccc3\" :question/math-academy-id \"q-73718\" :question/problem \"$$\\n\\\\displaystyle \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{5|x|\\\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\n$$\" :question/worked-solution \"Note that we can rewrite this integral as\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{5|x|\\\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}=\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}.\\n$$\\n\\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\\\text{arcsec},$\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\text{d}u=\\\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $5x.$\\n\\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{\\\\text{d}x}=5\\\\,⟹\\\\,\\\\text{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\text{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\begin{aligned}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{5|x|\\\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|5x|\\\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\text{d}x \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\\\cdot (\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\text{d}u) \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\int \\\\frac{\\\\text{d}u}{|u|\\\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\\\\\  & =\\\\frac{\\\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186676884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"093e8ee9-6706-5ac0-9856-c97b4df6f556\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676879} {:answer/id #uuid \"2d562848-1d97-52e5-9683-cb014d13bdb0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676903} {:answer/id #uuid \"520052f9-511f-5463-abd6-61c01b26c6c9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(81 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676927} {:answer/id #uuid \"7616d1f3-8012-52d1-b910-e3117af611f5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186676948} {:answer/id #uuid \"f781316b-ad0d-5599-b0d1-a715216cc7e8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{81}+C\" :db/id 17592186677032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2d562848-1d97-52e5-9683-cb014d13bdb0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676903} :answer-field/id #uuid \"60467e61-e7b2-548a-a8c4-112122fa9c9b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676938}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"1330265e-12c1-57f0-82dd-95378d9f20b0\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=9 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=9,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{9})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|9 x|=9|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{9}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9(\\\\frac{1}{9})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|9 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"20bf9841-2595-5f27-b0e8-1e9284708c28\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676896} {:answer/id #uuid \"6e42acbb-4f56-56be-a048-fba84c7dc573\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676942} {:answer/id #uuid \"7e019ca5-2476-5cb5-892a-c3f42ebb26e8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676954} {:answer/id #uuid \"b68e91f4-197a-5d0d-9aa6-776bde1a3333\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{64}+C\" :db/id 17592186676990} {:answer/id #uuid \"f2f477b1-1575-5b4e-ba38-698f5d0ef3a1\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"7e019ca5-2476-5cb5-892a-c3f42ebb26e8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676954} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f8007ccb-32ea-5c4e-8b8c-8bb848c4c191\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677033}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"184d3205-f072-5ec2-ae47-f41ae45b3346\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{8})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|8 x|=8|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{8}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1(\\\\frac{1}{8})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{1}{8}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{8}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|8 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"49ebbcc4-6039-5bf0-998a-dded9c3941e5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}}{14}+C\" :db/id 17592186676922} {:answer/id #uuid \"74cae605-ea8d-5ca5-8033-c10411a836ab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}}{196}+C\" :db/id 17592186676946} {:answer/id #uuid \"ab2399d7-22bf-5740-880c-727575b60c80\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676984} {:answer/id #uuid \"c7a55cec-6a4f-5cd8-bd20-ddc037f3250e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(196 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677007} {:answer/id #uuid \"eed14417-4f9a-5aae-9ec6-27bba65a8975\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"14 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ab2399d7-22bf-5740-880c-727575b60c80\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676984} :answer-field/id #uuid \"3494f9ef-9b8c-50b2-931e-8e49eba77f3b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676910}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"2c86da1f-3334-519e-bd8d-02dc5abc2552\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{14}{|14 x|\\\\sqrt{(14 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=14 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=14,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{14})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|14 x|=14|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{14}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{14}{|14 x|\\\\sqrt{(14 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 14\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|14 x|\\\\sqrt{(14 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 14(\\\\frac{1}{14})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(14 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|14 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0e0be1ee-1432-52ae-9e94-69b713d648c2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(121 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676880} {:answer/id #uuid \"59b25816-1279-51cb-af04-13bca7bd5f42\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}}{121}+C\" :db/id 17592186676933} {:answer/id #uuid \"626ff4e1-3b58-58c9-bc95-9f3d5bc3fad9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"11 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676939} {:answer/id #uuid \"b8d7fe7e-90a9-577a-92c4-5851d113ae44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}}{11}+C\" :db/id 17592186676992} {:answer/id #uuid \"f8e06bf5-bdcb-53e3-9ea8-e3b48ff07198\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"f8e06bf5-bdcb-53e3-9ea8-e3b48ff07198\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677035} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c8f4c10b-4483-58bc-be77-10c8b0e9c52b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677009}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"2cb5a03d-f884-5440-bad0-52e5f286b6f3\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{11}{|11 x|\\\\sqrt{(11 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=11 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=11,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{11})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|11 x|=11|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{11}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{11}{|11 x|\\\\sqrt{(11 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 11\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|11 x|\\\\sqrt{(11 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 11(\\\\frac{1}{11})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(11 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|11 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"11627a8d-6425-5a99-b9f4-e08ef26dbb78\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186676883} {:answer/id #uuid \"54c12a5d-b905-54d9-b018-d803a7bc0aa0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676930} {:answer/id #uuid \"5926164f-fed6-5e3a-ba40-860db0a5ab38\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{81}+C\" :db/id 17592186676932} {:answer/id #uuid \"66282b24-49ba-5f84-8c44-21e0d0e0baaf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186676940} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba323a7e-319b-5495-ba14-d1d7a671d138\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186676993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"11627a8d-6425-5a99-b9f4-e08ef26dbb78\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\" :db/id 17592186676883} :answer-field/id #uuid \"3cbd97b4-beaa-5e69-b275-d9ff5a285259\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676915}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"2ed62d92-c36a-50a5-9c81-caff226f716e\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=9 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=9,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{9})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|9 x|=9|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{9}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|9 x|\\\\sqrt{(9 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1(\\\\frac{1}{9})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{1}{9}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{9}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}}{9}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|9 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"52f20127-7026-51bd-b9eb-d3aaffbd7897\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186676928} {:answer/id #uuid \"a926cb91-61f3-563f-8349-379a686c3646\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"30 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676983} {:answer/id #uuid \"bab46891-026f-5774-bdfe-32c494dd6b77\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(36 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676995} {:answer/id #uuid \"c3d34534-5046-50b0-a039-b5b4e49d9381\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}}{36}+C\" :db/id 17592186677002} {:answer/id #uuid \"f8e644d1-662e-52e7-b469-8b247975de27\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"f8e644d1-662e-52e7-b469-8b247975de27\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677036} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6d4e21a5-098c-5819-b7c8-0666c70ecb95\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676941}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"3feb255f-aeba-5dbb-91d6-6231c18cb161\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{36 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=6 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=6,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{6})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|6 x|=6|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{6}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{36 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 30\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|6 x|\\\\sqrt{(6 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 30(\\\\frac{1}{6})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 5\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|6 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"15e65e07-085b-550a-a717-82d2d0a4449f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{64}+C\" :db/id 17592186676887} {:answer/id #uuid \"1d199601-926c-5873-9d3f-90aebc32fddf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676891} {:answer/id #uuid \"b71fa791-be0c-5a48-a50c-ab3294c89e93\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676991} {:answer/id #uuid \"e2e87151-dca4-5f40-a571-21cca555c271\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186677018} {:answer/id #uuid \"fc8cda26-f6db-5986-9ef8-10b89f69beda\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186677039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1d199601-926c-5873-9d3f-90aebc32fddf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676891} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4cebd2f9-e45b-5a2d-b6e5-c83b641f472b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676924}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"445c17c5-47bb-5095-a41c-cf964b636e04\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=8 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=8,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{8})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|8 x|=8|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{8}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|8 x|\\\\sqrt{(8 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9(\\\\frac{1}{8})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{9}{8}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{8}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|8 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0508ef6a-4649-544f-ab1c-27e5adee2091\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676878} {:answer/id #uuid \"5104680c-2ea7-5a28-9524-a65df4157530\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676926} {:answer/id #uuid \"88a8138f-4879-55af-97f9-f23b9b258f0e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{49}+C\" :db/id 17592186676963} {:answer/id #uuid \"99e9b877-5e59-5bba-9fdf-edd1082bc890\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676972} {:answer/id #uuid \"bd7d4e3d-f10d-50a1-949e-70eb132876dd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"99e9b877-5e59-5bba-9fdf-edd1082bc890\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676972} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f9c6d4df-1b11-5cdc-98b5-b254e3330011\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677037}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"56cb2a9f-1cff-57aa-9994-7646c802ee0c\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=7 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=7,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|7 x|=7|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{7}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{1}{7}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{7}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|7 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676949 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"006b058a-8757-53b5-9e86-166b3bad3f57\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186676873} {:answer/id #uuid \"31a5ba68-5ac7-536c-8c41-f1a5e3abe4fd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676907} {:answer/id #uuid \"7f880d5c-a5a7-5504-b0fb-6f1cc67b05ee\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(16 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676957} {:answer/id #uuid \"cf8e4da3-3b7a-5c40-80b9-cdaba7d45e44\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{16}+C\" :db/id 17592186677010} {:answer/id #uuid \"d02f031d-3d68-5f84-adca-189e93f397fa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d02f031d-3d68-5f84-adca-189e93f397fa\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677012} :answer-field/id #uuid \"74bbe62f-70cb-5fd0-962c-4bb2778265f0\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676945}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"76457b92-955f-57c1-a7b4-2de23b67fcb9\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=4 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=4,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|4 x|=4|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{4}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 4\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 4(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|4 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"142408c4-a856-5ba3-9cb3-fdd989d60438\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676886} {:answer/id #uuid \"1d9079dc-e0e9-5883-9ee0-be4e84800886\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676892} {:answer/id #uuid \"4b039ee6-7d56-5a1f-923a-48cd9541fb4e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676923} {:answer/id #uuid \"c69ee190-e333-5892-a21c-1640d2670d8a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}}{3}+C\" :db/id 17592186677006} {:answer/id #uuid \"e88d8113-27e3-54e9-aa5a-f4c0374e5bd7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(9 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1d9079dc-e0e9-5883-9ee0-be4e84800886\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676892} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e0a36f36-3cca-5caf-af0f-d26099a43110\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677016}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"84c7e966-96b7-5e2c-ab4c-0d93d8c57026\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=3 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=3,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{3})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|3 x|=3|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{3}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{(3 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9(\\\\frac{1}{3})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 3\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|3 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"30aa92c4-ebd0-55bf-9c66-85ea2a24fa20\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"13 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676906} {:answer/id #uuid \"3a65b91e-5c21-5e2c-b3c6-a218b18b9bad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676914} {:answer/id #uuid \"50b95fae-4e0c-584b-8066-dbac126da0ec\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(169 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676925} {:answer/id #uuid \"c47a4090-08a3-5435-9bb8-44f2b4199fd6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}}{169}+C\" :db/id 17592186677003} {:answer/id #uuid \"e6780705-5037-5ae0-94fe-1022c619a279\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}}{13}+C\" :db/id 17592186677021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"3a65b91e-5c21-5e2c-b3c6-a218b18b9bad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676914} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e99fdc4d-6ccd-5f2c-9678-d7a78417090f\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677025}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"8bc2e902-71e9-5912-9706-6f6dd6006240\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{13}{|13 x|\\\\sqrt{(13 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=13 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=13,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{13})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|13 x|=13|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{13}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{13}{|13 x|\\\\sqrt{(13 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 13\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|13 x|\\\\sqrt{(13 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 13(\\\\frac{1}{13})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(13 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|13 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0f28e42b-8620-5ae1-8f04-805f88867c6c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676881} {:answer/id #uuid \"228bf48b-6c00-5de6-bd83-cd4703885c3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676897} {:answer/id #uuid \"75d06d6f-6fe5-5d6f-9007-78758ffc948c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676947} {:answer/id #uuid \"bc16c7b4-f2db-5f7c-a2ff-83546ce380d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676998} {:answer/id #uuid \"f3779970-0bfa-5296-b548-2b234032333d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"228bf48b-6c00-5de6-bd83-cd4703885c3b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676897} :answer-field/id #uuid \"77b14ff6-ee23-5c1a-82b3-746ee344c414\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676950}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"8ec467ed-a842-5743-90ea-dc3e43a5c825\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=2 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=2,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{2})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|2 x|=2|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{2}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8(\\\\frac{1}{2})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 4\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|2 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"4062c6f4-8073-59e2-8572-082fb67e86cd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676918} {:answer/id #uuid \"54a15aad-5ed5-5e4d-ba7e-1c0422c019cd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3 \\\\sqrt{3} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676929} {:answer/id #uuid \"95e14540-a907-57a9-af56-5c13e9653546\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\sqrt{3} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676970} {:answer/id #uuid \"d6b5ffaf-8545-5b67-a43e-b06901fddd7e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677014} {:answer/id #uuid \"f03be629-e361-57e1-aa79-d89c4c2e71ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"f03be629-e361-57e1-aa79-d89c4c2e71ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677027} :answer-field/id #uuid \"7c2ce00a-b685-5520-b2c9-cc2b514b71f2\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676953}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"9109a0e2-f715-5496-8bcd-2bf0c487318b\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|x|\\\\sqrt{3 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=\\\\sqrt{3} x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=\\\\sqrt{3},\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|\\\\sqrt{3} x|=\\\\sqrt{3}|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|x|\\\\sqrt{3 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\sqrt{3}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|\\\\sqrt{3} x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{3} x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\sqrt{3}(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 9\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{3} x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|\\\\sqrt{3} x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"13b0f660-67ce-59a2-9cf2-d36d0c375fff\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}}{100}+C\" :db/id 17592186676885} {:answer/id #uuid \"1d12d78c-c5a9-5229-adea-c3244ab0d11f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}}{10}+C\" :db/id 17592186676890} {:answer/id #uuid \"35f9913b-fc0f-5a49-9eda-f6cec6430dcd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"10 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676911} {:answer/id #uuid \"361c11c2-2fa8-565f-b175-a7e910e759d9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(100 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676912} {:answer/id #uuid \"ac14cc1a-0019-5315-94d9-d5219638bc74\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ac14cc1a-0019-5315-94d9-d5219638bc74\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676985} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d2cf0d9b-76d2-51ef-8dd1-3354fdaf72b5\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677013}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"97af9687-66c6-579d-97d7-01feb5f40f72\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{10}{|10 x|\\\\sqrt{(10 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=10 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=10,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{10})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|10 x|=10|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{10}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{10}{|10 x|\\\\sqrt{(10 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 10\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|10 x|\\\\sqrt{(10 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 10(\\\\frac{1}{10})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|10 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0126e7ef-2ec7-5d7f-a8d7-582407009616\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676874} {:answer/id #uuid \"26615563-e530-5544-b9f7-a24d5d7c3520\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{16}+C\" :db/id 17592186676898} {:answer/id #uuid \"87ac9755-9f76-571a-b175-02e2902b7b30\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"28 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676962} {:answer/id #uuid \"90251f4c-b8bc-5104-8144-8db40d11f9fe\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(16 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676966} {:answer/id #uuid \"b18c1e92-4fd6-59c3-8c51-39c8501f69d6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186676989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0126e7ef-2ec7-5d7f-a8d7-582407009616\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676874} :answer-field/id #uuid \"3e68b545-b7d2-58c5-8c66-984cc938eb0b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676916}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"9b337ff1-b6e2-5702-be8d-d982b1477cdc\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{7}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=4 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=4,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|4 x|=4|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{4}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{7}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 28\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 28(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 7\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|4 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"42e651b5-5ee7-5e53-9e60-c92338128ff0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186676919} {:answer/id #uuid \"5c828979-a664-5348-8e96-bb972e22d4d4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{42}+C\" :db/id 17592186676935} {:answer/id #uuid \"7be11b07-f96b-5a92-bd34-ccb6ddcb37ed\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{7 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186676952} {:answer/id #uuid \"801ef18d-69aa-5378-b58a-91d4d3f3528c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{294}+C\" :db/id 17592186676958} {:answer/id #uuid \"f3049055-8ee7-5042-830b-a03fcd46e4c2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(49 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186677030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"42e651b5-5ee7-5e53-9e60-c92338128ff0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186676919} :answer-field/id #uuid \"9c355901-1679-5d66-ba00-1c7d5b2850b1\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676974}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"a1e5824f-e979-5164-8706-b0c5bb4e54bf\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{6|x|\\\\sqrt{49 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=7 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=7,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|7 x|=7|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{7}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{6|x|\\\\sqrt{49 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{7}{6}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{7}{6}(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{1}{6}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{6}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|7 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0420b9b3-9028-5e27-bbba-45726475b49d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676877} {:answer/id #uuid \"5c8f252f-19a7-51d6-bf28-81657f02c35f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676936} {:answer/id #uuid \"5dce131d-6dd3-5b85-9b63-176d037ffa33\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}}{6}+C\" :db/id 17592186676937} {:answer/id #uuid \"84724433-c0c0-532e-a461-3914e4459162\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}}{36}+C\" :db/id 17592186676959} {:answer/id #uuid \"b10591d8-d226-5f76-8227-953214d235b0\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(36 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0420b9b3-9028-5e27-bbba-45726475b49d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676877} :answer-field/id #uuid \"7f1fa66e-78d1-5a82-b8dc-d4104836048b\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676955}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"a30037a2-ab18-570c-bcd0-bd4c474b9e6f\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{6}{|6 x|\\\\sqrt{(6 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=6 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=6,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{6})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|6 x|=6|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{6}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{6}{|6 x|\\\\sqrt{(6 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 6\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|6 x|\\\\sqrt{(6 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 6(\\\\frac{1}{6})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|6 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0208a87c-e72d-5553-95a3-88676b1900da\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186676875} {:answer/id #uuid \"20a8febd-4faa-5a89-a1b1-fc75ee1112f9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}}{4}+C\" :db/id 17592186676895} {:answer/id #uuid \"39669edf-52ed-591a-bc4f-05f46c11d86d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}}{8}+C\" :db/id 17592186676913} {:answer/id #uuid \"a1ad18ec-e783-5a5d-ab40-fe59997cffab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186676975} {:answer/id #uuid \"a63a8958-2bad-585b-b08f-b28fdffa096b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a1ad18ec-e783-5a5d-ab40-fe59997cffab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186676975} :answer-field/id #uuid \"95c1d718-179c-5ae2-9903-11398143c9ae\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"a8e1e0d2-fc46-5618-9a39-5e6fdde9fc87\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{2|x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=2 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=2,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{2})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|2 x|=2|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{2}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{1}{2|x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 1(\\\\frac{1}{2})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{2}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}}{2}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|2 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1e490206-6d56-5574-9453-0e68c12263f2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676894} {:answer/id #uuid \"2e5efafe-ae73-5971-940e-1cb481b504a2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676904} {:answer/id #uuid \"59ce4e9f-cf5b-5371-8bdb-f1cbcc591855\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676934} {:answer/id #uuid \"9129a361-2e73-5adc-96c4-fa751e6d00a4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}}{2}+C\" :db/id 17592186676968} {:answer/id #uuid \"c5017709-422a-585d-8e3d-c3340f483d10\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2 \\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2e5efafe-ae73-5971-940e-1cb481b504a2\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676904} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f25faa23-2594-5f40-ab0a-2ecce21fbb68\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677028}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"ad5586bd-92a8-50ea-bd0f-7fa1955e49e8\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=4 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=4,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|4 x|=4|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{4}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8(\\\\frac{1}{4})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 2\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 2 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|4 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186676997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"792218b4-1e15-5c28-b955-ccc4600c533e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5 \\\\sqrt{7} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676951} {:answer/id #uuid \"a25ceb1a-ae7b-523e-8bb7-b1cce00f19ea\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676978} {:answer/id #uuid \"a52357f1-a274-5f15-ace4-aa9303c50604\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\sqrt{7} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676980} {:answer/id #uuid \"bb1874bf-30c9-586f-9061-209cdbe0411e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676996} {:answer/id #uuid \"e2cd009b-8c17-5c70-87e8-7659d526c59f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e2cd009b-8c17-5c70-87e8-7659d526c59f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677017} :answer-field/id #uuid \"15f2c563-ad1d-5843-a270-e994aa71edcb\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676888}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"bbd7d173-e034-5432-834c-943bd6bc824e\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=\\\\sqrt{7} x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=\\\\sqrt{7},\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{7})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|\\\\sqrt{7} x|=\\\\sqrt{7}|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{5}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\sqrt{7}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|\\\\sqrt{7} x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{7} x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\sqrt{7}(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{7})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 5\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 5 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|\\\\sqrt{7} x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186677001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1e3c92a4-a7da-51b0-8625-d966303b5bd9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"20 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676893} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba9ea4eb-0793-5e14-bb35-81349da6a845\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676994} {:answer/id #uuid \"c566ac9c-ddcc-5843-b570-313dfc0d0833\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}}{5}+C\" :db/id 17592186677005} {:answer/id #uuid \"e626e4b2-798b-511a-9112-b64176edcf02\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677019} {:answer/id #uuid \"fab2d188-b643-5b6e-a5ee-efa3c8f819df\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ba9ea4eb-0793-5e14-bb35-81349da6a845\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676994} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d6e53eea-4a9c-579c-9473-40e52033ceba\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"c2cb4fba-879b-5b01-9945-6bb60bed682b\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{20}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=5 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=5,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{5})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|5 x|=5|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{5}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{20}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 20\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 20(\\\\frac{1}{5})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 4\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 4 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|5 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186677008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"040ea9c9-e715-507d-902d-bb71351804ed\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676876} {:answer/id #uuid \"335a8d6a-b4ec-5193-a45f-51bf7646df64\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\sqrt{7} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676908} {:answer/id #uuid \"6ec7ce1f-0eb4-59d3-a1a0-ac1e9f4398a9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\sqrt{7} \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676943} {:answer/id #uuid \"e645444e-55cd-5743-bd4c-ad58f4b945a5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186677020} {:answer/id #uuid \"f88a3601-88ce-58e0-8eaa-5fa3af7b4c28\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"040ea9c9-e715-507d-902d-bb71351804ed\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676876} :answer-field/id #uuid \"e8606212-bc9b-52ae-8e0c-294774fd2b98\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186677023}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"c8193b88-2105-5bfe-b1c9-66d6db09c1f6\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=\\\\sqrt{7} x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=\\\\sqrt{7},\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{7})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|\\\\sqrt{7} x|=\\\\sqrt{7}|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{9}{|x|\\\\sqrt{7 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\sqrt{7}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|\\\\sqrt{7} x|\\\\sqrt{(\\\\sqrt{7} x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\sqrt{7}(\\\\frac{\\\\sqrt{7}}{7})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 9\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= 9 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(\\\\sqrt{7} x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|\\\\sqrt{7} x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186677022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"26f6ae5e-13b1-5d98-ad21-85c5db855690\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676899} {:answer/id #uuid \"2cfb56c8-c193-500d-8069-1875caf5cdec\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676902} {:answer/id #uuid \"a2305993-b75e-568a-b17f-56fd24469b05\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676977} {:answer/id #uuid \"b05682a8-ee96-5382-b3bc-5a9f5f4c3460\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{49}+C\" :db/id 17592186676987} {:answer/id #uuid \"cf98bfc5-b321-5f5f-9e9b-a7a3431c3b74\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arctan}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186677011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"26f6ae5e-13b1-5d98-ad21-85c5db855690\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\" :db/id 17592186676899} :answer-field/id #uuid \"71ec24ab-1b85-5c39-bff9-ac067e868069\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676944}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"e7dddafc-acd5-5fc7-9ee2-2276b6e756b8\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=7 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=7,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|7 x|=7|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{7}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{8}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|7 x|\\\\sqrt{(7 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 8(\\\\frac{1}{7})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{8}{7}\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}}{7}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\frac{8 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(7 x \\\\right)}}{7}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|7 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186677040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1073775f-1bbc-52ab-8c7e-572379bc0994\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676882} {:answer/id #uuid \"4834c340-bc67-5aa0-8c75-aeeabb21803e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}}{15}+C\" :db/id 17592186676921} {:answer/id #uuid \"7f47e282-f70d-54a9-bb2f-de9b835c81b6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}}{225}+C\" :db/id 17592186676956} {:answer/id #uuid \"860f1311-ba28-51b2-8a6b-3ee81d4d44ef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"15 \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676961} {:answer/id #uuid \"c0dca4bf-534c-5c1e-9ec4-fff63a26e7ff\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(225 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186677000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"1073775f-1bbc-52ab-8c7e-572379bc0994\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186676882} :answer-field/id #uuid \"33d2c788-e730-5daf-8cfa-322e2c30fcdb\" :answer-field/key \"selection\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186676909}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"feb12510-c969-520b-8bb7-8c2c49a14e5f\" :question/problem \"Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{15}{|15 x|\\\\sqrt{(15 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Use the linear substitution $u=15 x.$ Then\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{\\\\mathrm{d}u}{\\\\mathrm{d}x}=15,\\\\qquad \\\\mathrm{d}x=(\\\\frac{1}{15})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\\n\\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\\n\\n$$\\n|u|=|15 x|=15|x|,\\\\qquad \\\\frac{1}{|x|}=\\\\frac{15}{|u|}.\\n$$\\n\\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute and evaluate:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}& \\\\int \\\\frac{15}{|15 x|\\\\sqrt{(15 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 15\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|15 x|\\\\sqrt{(15 x)^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\\\\  &= 15(\\\\frac{1}{15})\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= 1\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|u|\\\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C \\\\\\\\  &= \\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(15 x \\\\right)}+C\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|15 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals.\"} {:db/id 17592186678939 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"17e8cc9b-2090-546f-b5f6-63612df70c02\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678948} {:answer/id #uuid \"93d5b36f-fd95-59e6-942a-e49927311fc9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679028} {:answer/id #uuid \"b01a33d3-e49a-58de-8a8f-1f7783630836\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679046} {:answer/id #uuid \"c9c5e16a-fe3c-5a7a-9b04-ffc25deaf432\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679067} {:answer/id #uuid \"dc24f586-1089-577f-8c0e-7f39b8c84c5c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"dc24f586-1089-577f-8c0e-7f39b8c84c5c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679080} :answer-field/id #uuid \"70a32f43-6d04-5912-9359-a8d23281df9b\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679009}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"062650d4-1fa4-5f2c-84e7-e8520dfa7735\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $4>0$, $|u|=4|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/4$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $16\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=4$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=4\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n4\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186678946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"44e17a93-4b68-5f97-8d11-f86308e07ed7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678979} {:answer/id #uuid \"5cf0f831-44b4-5b73-a24c-dd7052978071\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{8}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678995} {:answer/id #uuid \"9292dbeb-04c1-5a32-825d-48db9072d490\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679027} {:answer/id #uuid \"b38d76bb-3a13-5edd-b277-e294d22f2520\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679050} {:answer/id #uuid \"f1b16480-9c36-50f9-807e-8bef4c87f22a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679094}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b38d76bb-3a13-5edd-b277-e294d22f2520\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679050} :answer-field/id #uuid \"3db76bd0-786f-52f1-ae29-26420c6d4c60\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678971}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"129dd18f-6700-5ffb-9ca8-25a04326a78f\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=\\\\frac{1}{4}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186678964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0af9ecf0-ad27-5c54-bcc2-d7c243cc178e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678942} {:answer/id #uuid \"7919f065-684f-5162-84c1-326bee6ae511\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679015} {:answer/id #uuid \"876f62f1-9b04-5c3d-8733-6432cf43bea5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679023} {:answer/id #uuid \"91a06352-fe59-5083-972f-300fef7dbc84\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679026} {:answer/id #uuid \"b7a75978-9c9e-57e7-9d29-c8315015fdcd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679054}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"876f62f1-9b04-5c3d-8733-6432cf43bea5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679023} :answer-field/id #uuid \"2a5b0386-1523-52c2-8e5e-63a3e9478c59\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678962}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"2c09025a-e36a-5f98-8a3a-ecae05ef8ee0\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $4>0$, $|u|=4|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/4$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $12\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=3$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186678974 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"3ce6bf5b-cf0f-5180-b4bf-631b1a709785\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186678970} {:answer/id #uuid \"bce79f81-d030-503c-a803-5412bb4059cc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679058} {:answer/id #uuid \"c943b728-62d2-511e-a97a-4a0493bfe0ae\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679066} {:answer/id #uuid \"cc2c6c38-3869-5854-bef0-07369ed45e1a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679069} {:answer/id #uuid \"d0da665b-b83b-5950-a555-b72bb07169c9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"cc2c6c38-3869-5854-bef0-07369ed45e1a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679069} :answer-field/id #uuid \"ca7ef265-9e84-5525-8060-360e20887c13\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679068}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"40993577-26ec-5c2a-86d9-4cbecdb4a736\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $3>0$, $|u|=3|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/3$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186678978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5ddf65e8-eb2f-53be-ae83-c354ca054f8d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678996} {:answer/id #uuid \"6967a641-edd3-5a74-b591-85d1ab4da76f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679004} {:answer/id #uuid \"97ad9c8e-c2ce-5cb3-8b19-7f98b2f70e4d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679030} {:answer/id #uuid \"9e357565-9807-57f4-aab7-b7ef5b4f78bb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679033} {:answer/id #uuid \"c4ad03ca-167e-50ec-870b-d6819e0e5125\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"9e357565-9807-57f4-aab7-b7ef5b4f78bb\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679033} :answer-field/id #uuid \"50cd4bf5-1aa1-5030-84b4-a8276fb8ef30\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678989}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"42e86bff-6aba-589f-8a54-c26a0ba84936\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=\\\\frac{4}{5}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186678988 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"49bceb23-39fc-5501-8de2-bae684444332\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678983} {:answer/id #uuid \"5452d27c-098b-5d42-9957-4a9b29ed171c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678990} {:answer/id #uuid \"5562ca8a-35d2-531a-8583-831dbb8b4782\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678991} {:answer/id #uuid \"d4751077-0a7e-5a34-ba09-0f8a920a221c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679078} {:answer/id #uuid \"f804bd82-51d1-5855-8258-16ab61cd35c4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d4751077-0a7e-5a34-ba09-0f8a920a221c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679078} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6c4324ae-8174-549e-97e3-083fce1aac61\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679007}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"4fd16f91-5d8a-57c8-9912-b9ef2cf158ea\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=5 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=\\\\frac{2}{5}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"48e1bae3-16e7-5573-8ec1-32d48bb60bf6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186678982} {:answer/id #uuid \"7aa9a9e2-e7ca-568f-8ff8-ed126c211b80\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679017} {:answer/id #uuid \"a256a3dc-a3b6-5a7c-b4c9-2b41b4a45257\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679036} {:answer/id #uuid \"acaba63a-57d4-55fc-a498-65e838bc5d96\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679043} {:answer/id #uuid \"ce92345c-fccd-5f71-80c8-5f31cd57e8b6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"acaba63a-57d4-55fc-a498-65e838bc5d96\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679043} :answer-field/id #uuid \"bc353288-5fbe-520a-92d8-6ad2def9f414\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679057}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"69248dc5-2b73-53df-a95f-0df952ca5485\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=\\\\frac{1}{2}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"10dd7ff4-4d3d-5299-aa4f-53b2c52090f6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678945} {:answer/id #uuid \"21106588-e506-5e45-b746-8470cc41d3d3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678952} {:answer/id #uuid \"88b1adb7-c539-5b17-94fb-7c98350ca7bc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{10}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679024} {:answer/id #uuid \"94e86255-c299-5518-ba2c-4269426f2a23\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679029} {:answer/id #uuid \"a2644a79-8d95-5309-ba22-62887c805494\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"10dd7ff4-4d3d-5299-aa4f-53b2c52090f6\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678945} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d4272cb6-e3f1-54ab-83c8-24c8e6312246\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679077}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"79fd25dc-fe7a-5e6d-9af8-52074c40dff4\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=5 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=\\\\frac{1}{5}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1cc8a31c-bd74-5d67-b8a7-9c5e1ca9932a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678949} {:answer/id #uuid \"2adadd25-d5e5-5ebd-bbc3-59c1cd49688f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\" :db/id 17592186678963} {:answer/id #uuid \"5ae0933c-6d68-5428-8481-eb90fd459bb4\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678993} {:answer/id #uuid \"d5aeb8b6-1c02-5992-a768-3a79b93fa593\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679079} {:answer/id #uuid \"f6567fff-8697-5993-8738-f48f20019ac7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2adadd25-d5e5-5ebd-bbc3-59c1cd49688f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\" :db/id 17592186678963} :answer-field/id #uuid \"f336a66b-25b0-55c1-93aa-4c6a2e4cd416\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679096}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"7d2ee89d-6c8a-53ca-bf9f-9ef7347384d0\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=2 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"06b6f683-62bf-5a71-a0bf-5f5d78b13621\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678940} {:answer/id #uuid \"24beca5b-1bbc-564b-9111-b57262bf1a93\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678958} {:answer/id #uuid \"35a499f0-74ec-58b5-9289-81cd6de2ed8b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678967} {:answer/id #uuid \"5b37ef5c-0a54-50f9-8929-55db42f1cf0b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678994} {:answer/id #uuid \"fb47295e-82b8-5ceb-8a04-f8c683d541af\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679100}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"24beca5b-1bbc-564b-9111-b57262bf1a93\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678958} :answer-field/id #uuid \"6fb2c974-04f6-5efb-b7dc-3b38c233fb1b\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"81ad82b8-f4e0-58fa-accc-ffa4bebb139c\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=\\\\frac{4}{3}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679032 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"202b6e2e-f98c-5e7c-9e3a-d3c48dd60d36\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186678951} {:answer/id #uuid \"36f70c88-0ef6-5ca6-92e7-d158d89d5f26\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678968} {:answer/id #uuid \"8906364d-7222-5f86-b3ac-bbec3a33409f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679025} {:answer/id #uuid \"b2486e22-2554-5ff6-9d0b-18b86378bb57\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679048} {:answer/id #uuid \"d3a5cea4-702e-5fbb-950b-ef343585cf2a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"d3a5cea4-702e-5fbb-950b-ef343585cf2a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679076} :answer-field/id #uuid \"24b9be2c-5011-5f61-a5a7-479d6e9385a7\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678957}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"9c5c181d-b844-5b7d-9b79-1dad2f014764\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"41296916-dadd-5bca-b6b4-0766d5545441\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186678975} {:answer/id #uuid \"752db311-1066-5745-828f-5ec327c1bf77\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679011} {:answer/id #uuid \"78ca4bd8-5225-5b04-8a27-8d8cf24f20ad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679014} {:answer/id #uuid \"98955048-7c21-56c7-bf34-29aea44f1171\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679031} {:answer/id #uuid \"e84de875-40c5-5bdb-8a09-e48480956b35\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"752db311-1066-5745-828f-5ec327c1bf77\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679011} :answer-field/id #uuid \"2838d84b-328c-5b8b-bbf8-043a80c2dbeb\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"a18b62e4-bd0f-5ad5-a4da-6ae883771ad9\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $2>0$, $|u|=2|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/2$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{|x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679052 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"252218ad-1c4a-5fdb-acf3-685f2dad3a6e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678959} {:answer/id #uuid \"47e15b9f-f50c-567d-a1f5-f944fe687c5d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678980} {:answer/id #uuid \"75324eed-948f-5ad8-9539-9da66354e951\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679012} {:answer/id #uuid \"a731f87b-217d-5532-bca4-d095f70ce817\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679039} {:answer/id #uuid \"eab7f8bb-b962-515d-ae13-5b90b484af60\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"47e15b9f-f50c-567d-a1f5-f944fe687c5d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678980} :answer-field/id #uuid \"c369d541-d031-5b92-b58f-6c2a22c6752d\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679062}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"b663b9ed-8aa3-50e4-9703-f86bb3d5df61\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $5>0$, $|u|=5|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/5$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $15\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=3$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n3\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"423cac0f-e0d4-5c82-a36c-3fd77bc79d7e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678976} {:answer/id #uuid \"4256fa28-48a7-5d50-a4f2-714dd6256373\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678977} {:answer/id #uuid \"6b5c2a97-06ea-5deb-9a32-167c5fcf621d\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679006} {:answer/id #uuid \"70e8de43-8fdf-5b62-a70c-558d5960567c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679010} {:answer/id #uuid \"fd7d10e5-ea3f-530b-b2ab-a76c1cfd107c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"423cac0f-e0d4-5c82-a36c-3fd77bc79d7e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678976} :answer-field/id #uuid \"13e879be-7fd7-5b58-aac6-1b0f6a224e96\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678947}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"bfa0ba88-cd1a-5014-a502-27b6d9f6c943\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $3>0$, $|u|=3|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/3$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $6\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=2$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0858e303-d45b-544b-a82f-2b47d25c2485\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678941} {:answer/id #uuid \"76f48c92-d114-574e-949d-dfbbe632e2f7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{8}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679013} {:answer/id #uuid \"a979c3cc-5cec-59fa-9c86-1af8788026cf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679040} {:answer/id #uuid \"b6a37988-d4d9-5cc3-8d7e-644229205fc3\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679053} {:answer/id #uuid \"f9070c8e-98bb-537d-936c-b2fa536149cf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{9}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"a979c3cc-5cec-59fa-9c86-1af8788026cf\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679040} :answer-field/id #uuid \"cf2b3d6b-da18-5e5b-884b-0d11d69182a3\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679072}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"c0a73bc4-4368-5161-9323-4a7cdf99addc\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=\\\\frac{3}{4}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679063 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0c1ac374-c413-5ca4-9f1f-661629c2c5ca\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678943} {:answer/id #uuid \"23f84d1d-f503-59bc-99f2-653086abbd50\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\" :db/id 17592186678956} {:answer/id #uuid \"5616b423-4249-5fab-90b8-d2c73b2c6e24\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"6\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678992} {:answer/id #uuid \"7f83b197-1529-5e99-b04a-707f0a67cb4a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679019} {:answer/id #uuid \"d0aaf219-cc1f-5535-8fd4-5d943078d5b9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"0c1ac374-c413-5ca4-9f1f-661629c2c5ca\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678943} :answer-field/id #uuid \"a58d8e6b-747b-566c-b93f-043f949d5404\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679038}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"c4638d6c-303b-5cb5-b68d-3da8c48514be\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=2 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}=2$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"5f66405d-f8fd-5913-9c55-7a2a881e0f3c\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186678997} {:answer/id #uuid \"5fe273df-1eda-5c72-9f41-fe06a6624c7a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678998} {:answer/id #uuid \"8739ebb0-2e91-578e-934b-e2ab9dcce44b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679022} {:answer/id #uuid \"b1dd7846-263d-5ecc-9848-7ddcd4fec346\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679047} {:answer/id #uuid \"bb86e264-e9b1-5a13-bdad-5916b0ae8452\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"8739ebb0-2e91-578e-934b-e2ab9dcce44b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C\" :db/id 17592186679022} :answer-field/id #uuid \"05742652-f2f3-5e0c-9369-fff85f913bff\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678938}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"c517ee8b-2398-5c31-9dd5-72e74530ca24\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=2 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(2)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|2 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{2}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|2 x|\\\\sqrt{4 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(2 x \\\\right)}+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679070 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"1e6cf756-f438-5468-b2ac-a1a776c0186b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678950} {:answer/id #uuid \"2edf2af8-329a-558f-9a49-44d53d51089a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\" :db/id 17592186678966} {:answer/id #uuid \"3e474cd7-7f34-5a64-bab1-3c3a2b0f75b8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678972} {:answer/id #uuid \"674b7b7c-6378-5abc-9d6c-fc9b19a1f412\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"3\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679002} {:answer/id #uuid \"fe63a10d-a712-51b7-9c53-b15089294653\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-1\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"2edf2af8-329a-558f-9a49-44d53d51089a\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\" :db/id 17592186678966} :answer-field/id #uuid \"01af17da-f496-51ca-bfbc-212a3fe55113\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678937}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"cc70bb19-41c8-5bc7-bc7b-7067838806aa\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=1$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"23ae40c8-dc38-59a6-bf33-5dcd76ff572b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678955} {:answer/id #uuid \"61691232-1c0b-5613-ba64-028cfeb6e4c5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"8\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678999} {:answer/id #uuid \"61b30356-4581-5a04-8e9e-e9f024e0634f\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679000} {:answer/id #uuid \"b29f38ea-83ae-5fe9-b85c-022cd5e0b555\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679049} {:answer/id #uuid \"efbbcdac-6022-538c-b9c9-08cbc5bab89b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"b29f38ea-83ae-5fe9-b85c-022cd5e0b555\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679049} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4e83d6e8-b921-5001-9022-b4bf4f708392\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678987}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"e0ca915f-85de-5d80-bc7b-4f29aece6b54\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $3>0$, $|u|=3|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/3$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $12\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=4$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=4\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n4\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679082 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"0cfa16d4-5631-5ba3-934a-4410fa770adc\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678944} {:answer/id #uuid \"482a3659-7a22-5e4c-8b9a-2a39a7fc8886\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186678981} {:answer/id #uuid \"bee12273-2a83-5105-b4c7-86e2a206049b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679059} {:answer/id #uuid \"f16dfa66-8c67-52e6-a66a-7a95a8924434\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{12}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679093} {:answer/id #uuid \"fbcd31a5-5b5e-57da-8f89-9460b07dd7d5\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{8}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"bee12273-2a83-5105-b4c7-86e2a206049b\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)\" :db/id 17592186679059} :answer-field/id #uuid \"a1e2a447-4272-5a1e-a954-82d13a7c6622\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid \"e3061ebb-f317-5736-bf9c-2f1ab8d1fb2b\" :question/problem \"Use the substitution $u=5 x$. Which integral is obtained?\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $4\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=\\\\frac{4}{5}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{4}{|5 x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nThe transformed integral is\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{4}{5}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"23088978-2ce1-5552-a18e-32ab1b227133\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"-2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678954} {:answer/id #uuid \"2867c5f9-486e-5412-9dc6-3f424ccb2821\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678961} {:answer/id #uuid \"4d0cd5f7-073d-5d5a-b881-bdaaeaaf2053\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678985} {:answer/id #uuid \"ab0bce01-5c37-5eef-acfa-6c3ad9b30c48\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"4\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679041} {:answer/id #uuid \"ecfeba93-2ccd-5d4f-bebf-35393b80e906\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"4d0cd5f7-073d-5d5a-b881-bdaaeaaf2053\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678985} :answer-field/id #uuid \"37c1b041-26d8-547b-afc4-f26c60dc9ce0\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678969}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid \"e458c6a7-d57b-5820-90ef-f845411de6d9\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=5 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(5)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|5 x|>1$.\\n\\nBecause $5>0$, $|u|=5|x|$, so $|x|=|u|/5$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $10\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{5}=2$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|x|\\\\sqrt{25 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n2\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"2c2e2a1a-3cd6-5c4c-aebd-51d8adce6fcd\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678965} {:answer/id #uuid \"ae144fb9-7aa6-577c-afcc-9db6f4da3b89\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{2}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679044} {:answer/id #uuid \"ae2a61db-1b69-5e72-b058-0c91779f9cde\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679045} {:answer/id #uuid \"e740253a-8298-550f-879e-caa0ff00a294\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(8 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679084} {:answer/id #uuid \"e923fc12-9cee-5e6f-b8ea-abccf7941fef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"e923fc12-9cee-5e6f-b8ea-abccf7941fef\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679086} :answer-field/id #uuid \"b3e9108b-9b5d-5ac8-beba-3e637f2e5c1b\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"f054d58c-180c-591b-ad06-4546c86b706b\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{4}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $3\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{4}=\\\\frac{3}{4}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{3}{|4 x|\\\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{3}{4}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(4 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"22234917-661d-55e6-bf15-1539dc6f1ca9\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(6 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678953} {:answer/id #uuid \"40598f69-d38c-580a-ac76-25dd1df1772e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678973} {:answer/id #uuid \"4c5be87a-280e-5e27-94d4-760eb3e4efab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{4}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678984} {:answer/id #uuid \"61ea967d-3662-5112-a401-c106190ec2d8\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679001} {:answer/id #uuid \"ba785ef5-5dfe-56a4-9972-ec65ecf92308\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"40598f69-d38c-580a-ac76-25dd1df1772e\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186678973} :answer-field/id #uuid \"d20f1c0e-2f95-59e8-aaf0-a406d464023a\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186679075}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid \"f0669784-ec1f-5ea5-8858-d62b3e3c7a46\" :question/problem \"Find an antiderivative.\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\n$$\\n\\nYou may use $\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u=\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}+C$.\\n\\nWork on a connected interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution \"Let $u=3 x$. Then $\\\\mathrm{d}u=(3)\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x$.\\n\\nWork on a connected real interval where $|3 x|>1$.\\n\\nThe differential is $\\\\mathrm{d}x=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $2\\\\cdot \\\\frac{1}{3}=\\\\frac{2}{3}$.\\n\\nIncluding the differential factor gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\begin{aligned}&\\\\int \\\\frac{2}{|3 x|\\\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\\\&=\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right).\\\\end{aligned}\\n$$\\n\\nUse the supplied primitive:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\int \\\\frac{1}{\\\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\\\left|{u}\\\\right|}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}u\\\\right)=\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(u \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\\n\\nSubstitute back:\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(3 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C.\\n$$\"} {:db/id 17592186679095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid \"696e45a1-fd5f-57d8-9430-112536a04978\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(10 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679005} {:answer/id #uuid \"821b7127-b355-5427-a9ef-1b1dac049cab\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679021} {:answer/id #uuid \"ac964986-401f-564c-b1a5-b2b673875903\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679042} {:answer/id #uuid \"ed85456d-5678-5a66-b5ec-36790d6f87d7\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"- \\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679089} {:answer/id #uuid \"fd8e0c30-f35d-5003-a4dd-9448e64631ad\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{6}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid \"ac964986-401f-564c-b1a5-b2b673875903\" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value \"\\\\frac{3}{5}\\\\left(\\\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\\\left(5 x \\\\right)}\\\\right)+C\" :db/id 17592186679042} :answer-field/id #uuid \"4d199d5d-0de4-57e8-9e25-af029988c010\" :answer-field/key \"answer\" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186678986}